Question: 7 Display Numbers in Sorted Order

Scenario: A teacher enters students' marks, but some marks are repeated. Write a Java program using a TreeSet to display the unique marks in ascending order.





Solution:
import java.util.*;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        TreeSet<Integer> marks = new TreeSet<>();

        marks.add(80);
        marks.add(90);
        marks.add(70);
        marks.add(80);
        marks.add(60);
        marks.add(90);

        System.out.println("Sorted Unique Marks: " + marks);
    }
}
